```
VERDICT_TOP3:
1. mudwell — "well" as the source/a watering hole, also evokes "wish well" for rebirth — works because it's short, slug-safe, mildly mythic, and reads as "well-mud" or "mud-well" without vulgarity; suggests a deep, trustworthy place clients draw from.
2. mudgate — straight gateway metaphor for site-mode proxy — works because it tells the truth (operator gateway at mud.revivalworld.org), one word, npm-safe, no cultural baggage, and pairs naturally with future "mudgate-player".
3. rerite — reb(irth) + rite/rite-of-passage, nod to zMUD lineage (z→re) — works because it's bilingual-friendly (重生之禮), product-agnostic beyond Revival World, and frames MUDing as ritual rather than a dorky acronym.

ALSO_GOOD:
- mudway — "way/path" + 道路, echoes RW navigation/road meta
- ziren — 子認 / 子任, plays on zMUD's "z" and "任/認" (to take responsibility for), very Chinese-flavored codename
- tethermud — "tethered" wire from browser→proxy→telnet, honest about thin client
- telmud — honest telnet-first branding, reads clean, easy to type
- mudloom — loom weaves sessions/scripts together, evokes the scripting engine

AVOID:
- mudhub — screams "generic github template #47", no soul
- mudly / mudder — too close to "smudly" / Reddit's r/mudder, sounds like a cleaning product
- mudforge — overloaded with gaming-cliché fantasy tone, pretentious for a proxy
- mudshell — collides hard with "mush" reading and existing shell tools
- zMud2 / zmud-ng — trademark-adjacent, arrogant, and locks you to one ancestor
- mudgatekeeper — too long, sounds like a CAPTCHA product
- revivalmud — fine name but literally a one-campaign brand; paints you into RW corner

CHINESE_PRODUCT_TITLE: 重生之徑 — "Path of Rebirth". Reads as 道路/navigation (your map feature), rebirth (your benchmark), and 徑 has a classical MUD-literature feel without being limited to 復活世界. Falls back gracefully to 通境之門 ("Gateway of Realms") if you want a more operator-flavored title.

ONE_LINE: mudwell — high confidence; short, slug-safe, gateway+depth metaphor, survives the "assMud" rebrand cleanly and works whether you ever ship player mode or pivot past Revival World.
```